  "goodToKnow": "Die Schließung is the closure of a shop, school, factory or border: die Schließung der Grenze, die Schließung des Werks. It describes the act, usually the official one. For a daily closing (a shop shutting for the night), German says Ladenschluss or Feierabend. Note the ß after the long ie: Schließung, schließen. In Switzerland, where ß isn't used, it's written Schliessung."
